window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-0e404eb0382e6d74"]={"key":"ny_b1-0e404eb0382e6d74","group":"ny_b1","uid":"0e404eb0382e6d74","rank":48,"title":"real estate vendor termination notice 001","occupation":"concierges","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Tamsin Kilgore, the enterprise concierge lead at Saltcombe Consortium, and Selma Tikhonov needs a formal notice sent to Ravensmoor Freight this week. Saltcombe uses Ravensmoor for resident and prospect airport transfers under a livery services agreement signed on 1 January 2025. The relationship has broken down after four documented no-shows: the 14 April, 9 May, 21 June, and 2 August airport or resident-transfer bookings. The 21 June failure involved a prospect who then leased elsewhere, and two resident events are still scheduled for later this month. Saltcombe has paid the £4,800 monthly retainer through 31 December 2025, but the business now intends to end the arrangement four months early, effective 31 August 2025, and recover the portion that was prepaid for September through December. Prepare the termination notice itself, addressed to Ravensmoor Freight’s owner, using England and Wales as the jurisdiction and 15 August 2025 as the date of the notice. The agreement’s relevant provisions are clause 7.1, which requires a written notice describing a material service failure and gives five business days to cure where cure is reasonably possible, clause 9.2, which permits termination for repeated material failure after the cure opportunity, and clause 10.4, which requires reconciliation and repayment of prepaid fees for services not delivered after termination; the notice and cure provisions must be referred to precisely rather than paraphrased into a different obligation. Please produce two versions of the same final letter: an editable Word file named `saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.docx` and a matching PDF named `saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.pdf`, both written into the top level of the working directory where you start. 1) State the parties, agreement date, notice date, effective termination date, service failures, and the contractual provisions relied upon. 2) Make clear why the four failures are being treated as repeated material failures, while distinguishing the missed prospect transfer from a claim that cannot be proved from the facts provided. 3) Address the two upcoming resident events without promising service, cancellation, replacement transport, or any other obligation that the agreement does not already impose. 4) Set out the retainer reconciliation clearly: show the monthly amount, the four unearned months, and the total repayment sought, and explain the calculation so that a reviewer can reproduce it. 5) Give Ravensmoor a practical way to acknowledge receipt and identify any factual dispute, but do not turn the letter into a negotiation, a tutorial on contract law, or a general operating procedure. The usual assumption that a vendor receives a routine notice period does not fit this situation because the agreement contains a repeated-failure termination route and the stated cure opportunity has already been relevant to the service history; handle that tension explicitly and accurately. The owner may not know Saltcombe’s internal compliance terminology, so write plainly enough for that reader while retaining the precision an auditor would expect. Keep the letter to two pages or fewer, use a final and professional register, do not cite live sources or invent facts, and end with the decision and repayment demand rather than a list of future actions.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.docx` — Editable formal vendor termination notice addressed to Ravensmoor Freight and issued by Saltcombe Consortium. (Must be a complete letter, not a memo or procedure.; Must be no more than two pages.; Must contain the same factual content and figures as the PDF.; Must be suitable for sending after ordinary internal review.)\n- `saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.pdf` — Matching final PDF rendering of the editable termination notice. (Must reproduce the same letter as the DOCX.; Must be no more than two pages.; Dates, clause references, amounts, and termination decision must agree with the DOCX.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.docx","bytes":39886,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/afa6e4ec9e990146f8126be75c091b90b112cd7f13162ccbbea71c9323296ce7.docx","sha256":"afa6e4ec9e990146f8126be75c091b90b112cd7f13162ccbbea71c9323296ce7","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"15 August 2025\nFor the attention of: Owner\nRavensmoor Freight\nBy reply to the sending email / usual contract correspondence channel\nFORMAL NOTICE: TERMINATION OF LIVERY SERVICES AGREEMENT\nDear Owner,\nSaltcombe Consortium gives Ravensmoor Freight formal written notice that the livery services agreement signed on 1 January 2025 (the \"Agreement\") will terminate on 31 August 2025. This notice is issued under the laws and jurisdiction of England and Wales.\nService failures\nRavensmoor did not attend four booked airport or resident transfers: 14 April 2025, 9 May 2025, 21 June 2025, and 2 August 2025. These are recorded as no-shows. The 21 June failure involved a prospect; that prospect subsequently leased elsewhere. Saltcombe records that sequence as a business outcome, but does not assert that the no-show legally caused the lost lease.\nTaken together, four failures across the service period are being treated as repeated material failures. Reliable attendance is the central purpose of these bookings, and the recurrence has materially undermined the service relationship, including the prospect experience and resident service confidence.\nContractual basis and finality\nUnder clause 7.1, written notice must describe a material service failure and five business days are allowed to cure where cure is reasonably possible. The service history above has already provided the relevant opportunity to address the attendance failures; this notice does not create a new cure period or a new contractual condition. Clause 9.2 permits termination for repeated material failure after that cure opportunity, and Saltcombe is exercising that route.\nThe ordinary expectation of a routine notice period is therefore not the operative basis for this decision. The Agreement's repeated-failure route has been engaged, rather than a routine convenience termination. Termination is final and takes effect on 31 August 2025; it is not conditional on Ravensmoor's acknowledgment, agreement, or payment.\nUpcoming resident events\nTwo resident events remain scheduled for later in August. They are noted here for an accurate record only. This notice does not promise that Ravensmoor will perform either event, does not promise replacement transport, and does not state that either event is cancelled. No additional service commitment is created by this notice.\nRetainer reconciliation and repayment\nUnearned period\nMonthly retainer\nAmount prepaid\nSeptember 2025\n£4,800\n£4,800\nOctober 2025\n£4,800\n£4,800\nNovember 2025\n£4,800\n£4,800\nDecember 2025\n£4,800\n£4,800\nTotal repayment sought\n£4,800 × 4\n£19,200\nSaltcombe paid the £4,800 monthly retainer through 31 December 2025. Under clause 10.4, the prepaid fees for services not delivered after termination must be reconciled and repaid. The unearned period is September through December 2025: £4,800 per month × 4 months = £19,200. Saltcombe therefore demands repayment of £19,200 as prepaid and unearned after termination, not as a discretionary refund.\nPlease acknowledge receipt by replying to the sending email and identify any specific factual dispute, if applicable. Acknowledgment is requested for the record and is not a condition of termination.\nAccordingly, the Agreement terminates on 31 August 2025 under clause 9.2, and £19,200 is due to Saltcombe Consortium under clause 10.4 for the four unearned prepaid months.\nYours faithfully,\nTamsin Kilgore\nEnterprise Concierge Lead\nFor Saltcombe Consortium","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.pdf","bytes":46107,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/b927cef81e98ba2d536cd762178ee20e8132faa17a5d20e0417b55e5c6a390b4.pdf","sha256":"b927cef81e98ba2d536cd762178ee20e8132faa17a5d20e0417b55e5c6a390b4","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"                                                                                   SALTCOMBE CONSORTIUM\n                                                                                             15 August 2025\nFor the attention of: Owner\nRavensmoor Freight\nBy reply to the sending email / usual contract correspondence channel\n\nFORMAL NOTICE: TERMINATION OF LIVERY SERVICES AGREEMENT\nDear Owner,\nSaltcombe Consortium gives Ravensmoor Freight formal written notice that the livery services agreement\nsigned on 1 January 2025 (the \"Agreement\") will terminate on 31 August 2025. This notice is issued under the\nlaws and jurisdiction of England and Wales.\nService failures\nRavensmoor did not attend four booked airport or resident transfers: 14 April 2025, 9 May 2025, 21 June\n2025, and 2 August 2025. These are recorded as no-shows. The 21 June failure involved a prospect; that\nprospect subsequently leased elsewhere. Saltcombe records that sequence as a business outcome, but does\nnot assert that the no-show legally caused the lost lease.\nTaken together, four failures across the service period are being treated as repeated material failures.\nReliable attendance is the central purpose of these bookings, and the recurrence has materially undermined\nthe service relationship, including the prospect experience and resident service confidence.\nContractual basis and finality\nUnder clause 7.1, written notice must describe a material service failure and five business days are allowed to\ncure where cure is reasonably possible. The service history above has already provided the relevant\nopportunity to address the attendance failures; this notice does not create a new cure period or a new\ncontractual condition. Clause 9.2 permits termination for repeated material failure after that cure opportunity,\nand Saltcombe is exercising that route.\nThe ordinary expectation of a routine notice period is therefore not the operative basis for this decision. The\nAgreement's repeated-failure route has been engaged, rather than a routine convenience termination.\nTermination is final and takes effect on 31 August 2025; it is not conditional on Ravensmoor's\nacknowledgment, agreement, or payment.\nUpcoming resident events\nTwo resident events remain scheduled for later in August. They are noted here for an accurate record only.\nThis notice does not promise that Ravensmoor will perform either event, does not promise replacement\ntransport, and does not state that either event is cancelled. No additional service commitment is created by\nthis notice.\nRetainer reconciliation and repayment\n        Unearned period                                    Monthly retainer       Amount prepaid\n\n        September 2025                                     £4,800                 £4,800\n\n        October 2025                                       £4,800                 £4,800\n\n        November 2025                                      £4,800                 £4,800\n\n        December 2025                                      £4,800                 £4,800\n\n        Total repayment sought                             £4,800 × 4             £19,200\n\nSaltcombe paid the £4,800 monthly retainer through 31 December 2025. Under clause 10.4, the prepaid fees\nfor services not delivered after termination must be reconciled and repaid. The unearned period is September\nthrough December 2025: £4,800 per month × 4 months = £19,200. Saltcombe therefore demands repayment\nof £19,200 as prepaid and unearned after termination, not as a discretionary refund.\nPlease acknowledge receipt by replying to the sending email and identify any specific factual dispute, if\napplicable. Acknowledgment is requested for the record and is not a condition of termination.\nAccordingly, the Agreement terminates on 31 August 2025 under clause 9.2, and £19,200 is due to\nSaltcombe Consortium under clause 10.4 for the four unearned prepaid months.\n\nYours faithfully,\nTamsin Kilgore\nEnterprise Concierge Lead\nFor Saltcombe Consortium\n\n                          Saltcombe Consortium | Formal vendor notice | 15 August 2025\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter identifies Saltcombe Consortium and Ravensmoor Freight as the parties and identifies the agreement as dated 1 January 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening address, subject line, or first substantive paragraph.","grader_hint":"Confirm both organisation names and the agreement date appear unambiguously."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter is dated 15 August 2025.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Letter date.","grader_hint":"Check the displayed date, allowing equivalent day-month-year formatting."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter states that termination takes effect on 31 August 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Termination paragraph.","grader_hint":"The effective date must be expressed as the operative termination date, not merely as a scheduling reference."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter records all four no-show dates: 14 April, 9 May, 21 June, and 2 August 2025.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Factual chronology or enumerated service-failure passage.","grader_hint":"Count the distinct dates and verify that all four are present; equivalent date formats are acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter accurately states that the 21 June failure involved a prospect who subsequently leased elsewhere, without claiming that the no-show legally caused the lost lease.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Description of the 21 June incident.","grader_hint":"Credit a careful factual formulation such as 'the prospect then leased elsewhere'; reject unsupported causation presented as fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter cites clause 7.1 as the written material-service-failure notice and cure provision.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contractual-basis paragraph.","grader_hint":"The clause number and its relevant function must both be correctly connected."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter cites clause 9.2 as the repeated-material-failure termination provision.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contractual-basis paragraph.","grader_hint":"Do not credit a generic reference to 'the agreement' without the precise clause."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter cites clause 10.4 as the provision requiring reconciliation and repayment of prepaid fees for services not delivered after termination.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Repayment paragraph.","grader_hint":"Verify both the clause number and the repayment/reconciliation concept."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter explains that the ordinary expectation of a routine notice period is not the operative basis here because the agreement provides a repeated-failure termination route and the relevant cure opportunity has already been addressed in the service history.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Termination-basis explanation.","grader_hint":"Look for a concise explanation distinguishing ordinary notice from clause 9.2; do not require a particular phrase."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter states that the failures are being treated as repeated material failures rather than merely listing missed bookings.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reason for termination.","grader_hint":"The document should connect recurrence and service significance to the decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter uses a plain explanation of the cure position and does not expand the five-business-day cure language into a new cure period or new contractual condition.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Clause 7.1 discussion.","grader_hint":"Check that the letter acknowledges the cure provision without inviting a fresh cure process unless supported by the stated facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The repayment calculation shows £4,800 per month for four unearned months, September through December 2025, producing a total repayment demand of £19,200.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Retainer reconciliation table or prose calculation.","grader_hint":"Recalculate 4,800 × 4 and verify that the months are consecutive and begin after the 31 August termination date."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter clearly labels the £19,200 as prepaid and unearned after termination, rather than as a discretionary goodwill refund.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Repayment demand.","grader_hint":"The contractual character of the amount must be clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter addresses the two upcoming resident events without promising that Ravensmoor will perform them, promising replacement transport, or asserting that either event is cancelled.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Upcoming-events paragraph.","grader_hint":"Credit a bounded statement that the events remain noted and that no additional service commitment is created by the notice."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter provides a practical receipt or dispute-contact route without making acknowledgment a condition of termination.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Closing paragraph.","grader_hint":"An email or named business contact is sufficient; do not require invented contact details."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter is final and unambiguous that the agreement will terminate on 31 August 2025.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Overall letter language.","grader_hint":"Reject wording that makes termination conditional on acceptance, negotiation, payment, or acknowledgment."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The letter is written for a vendor owner with limited internal compliance background while remaining sufficiently precise for an auditor or oversight reviewer.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a non-specialist can understand the decision, dates, basis, and money claim without receiving a contract-law tutorial."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The letter does not overstate legal conclusions, statutory rights, causation, or facts not supplied in the brief.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document.","grader_hint":"Look especially for unsupported claims of damages, fraud, repudiation, statutory entitlement, or guaranteed lost business."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document is a self-contained formal notice rather than an SOP, explanatory memo, training handout, or negotiation script.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document.","grader_hint":"It should read as correspondence that can be sent to Ravensmoor, with normal letter conventions and no instructional sections."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each delivered version is no more than two pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX and PDF page counts.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX and inspect the PDF; both must be two pages or fewer."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX and PDF agree on every shared material figure and date, including £4,800, four months, £19,200, 15 August 2025, 31 August 2025, and the four incident dates.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Side-by-side comparison of both files.","grader_hint":"Extract text from both files and compare the listed figures, dates, clause references, and decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter invents or imposes a new operational obligation, such as requiring Ravensmoor to provide replacement transport, perform the two upcoming events, submit a new report, or follow a newly created handover procedure.","weight":-5.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document.","grader_hint":"Apply once for any material invented obligation; do not penalize a narrowly worded request to acknowledge receipt or identify a factual dispute."},{"rubric_item_id":"r23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The notice ends with the termination decision and repayment demand, not with a generic next-steps list or language suggesting that the decision remains open.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final paragraph and sign-off.","grader_hint":"The closing should reinforce finality and the amount sought."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"A real-estate concierge is preparing a formal vendor communication that ends a livery arrangement, records the contractual basis for the decision, and supports recovery of prepaid funds. The document must be operationally usable by the vendor and defensible to an auditor or compliance reviewer.","difficulty_sources":["material ambiguity about whether repeated service failures justify early contractual termination","need to distinguish an ordinary notice period from a termination-for-cause mechanism","need to recover an unearned prepaid retainer without creating a new payment or service obligation","need to write a final, audience-appropriate notice for a vendor owner while keeping it usable for compliance review","need to make two output formats agree on all dates and figures"],"authoring_plan":{"source_facts":{"client":"Saltcombe Consortium","vendor":"Ravensmoor Freight","agreement_date":"1 January 2025","notice_date":"15 August 2025","termination_date":"31 August 2025","monthly_retainer":4800,"unearned_months":["September 2025","October 2025","November 2025","December 2025"],"repayment_total":19200,"no_show_dates":["14 April 2025","9 May 2025","21 June 2025","2 August 2025"],"upcoming_events":2,"clauses":{"7.1":"written notice describing a material service failure and five-business-day cure where cure is reasonably possible","9.2":"termination for repeated material failure after the cure opportunity","10.4":"reconciliation and repayment of prepaid fees for services not delivered after termination"},"jurisdiction":"England and Wales"},"construction_requirements":["Create one polished formal letter and export the same content to DOCX and PDF.","Use a restrained subject line, date, recipient/address placeholders that do not invent a real address, salutation, concise factual chronology, contractual basis, termination statement, reconciliation, treatment of the two upcoming events, receipt/dispute contact route, and final sign-off.","State the four no-shows and the prospect outcome carefully, without asserting legal causation or unsupported damages.","Explain why the repeated-failure route, rather than an ordinary routine notice assumption, is being used, while preserving the exact supplied clause references.","Show the arithmetic as £4,800 × 4 = £19,200 and identify September through December as the unearned period.","Do not add a new service, handover, reporting, cancellation, replacement-transport, or payment-plan obligation.","Keep the rendered letter within two pages and ensure the PDF is a faithful rendering of the DOCX."],"gold_derivation":"The gold is a two-page-or-shorter final notice using only the supplied facts, with a clear immediate decision effective 31 August 2025, exact references to clauses 7.1, 9.2, and 10.4, a four-incident chronology, bounded treatment of the two upcoming events, and a reproducible £19,200 repayment calculation. Validate by text extraction, arithmetic recomputation, page-count inspection, and side-by-side DOCX/PDF comparison, followed by two independent professional reviews."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"termination_notice_docx","filename":"saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Editable formal vendor termination notice addressed to Ravensmoor Freight and issued by Saltcombe Consortium.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be a complete letter, not a memo or procedure.","Must be no more than two pages.","Must contain the same factual content and figures as the PDF.","Must be suitable for sending after ordinary internal review."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"termination_notice_pdf","filename":"saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"Matching final PDF rendering of the editable termination notice.","required":true,"constraints":["Must reproduce the same letter as the DOCX.","Must be no more than two pages.","Dates, clause references, amounts, and termination decision must agree with the DOCX."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"communicate_stakeholders","work_product":"operating_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"concierges","sector":"real_estate_rental_leasing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have a domain-experienced reviewer assess contractual precision, factual restraint, audience suitability, and finality; use offline document extraction and rendering to verify dates, arithmetic, page counts, filenames, and cross-format agreement.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No supplied contract is available, so clause language is evaluated against the contractual facts stated in the request rather than an external legal source.","The task is not a substitute for jurisdiction-specific legal advice; the artifact should avoid unsupported statutory conclusions."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:44:28+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:44:28+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:44:28+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:44:28+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['r04', 'r05', 'r08', 'r10']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:44:28+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/0e404eb0382e6d74","declared_deliverables":["saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.docx","saltcombe_ravensmoor_termination_notice.pdf"]};
